Hi everyone

Instats is excited to offer a new 4-part course, AI for Academic Research <https://instats.org/course/ai-for-writing-papers-and-analyzing-data1>. As artificial intelligence transforms academic research, this course provides PhD students, faculty, and professional researchers with practical skills for integrating AI into their research workflows responsibly and effectively. Moving beyond basic prompting, participants will learn to deploy AI agents to discover and critically evaluate literature, analyze data, develop manuscripts, and conduct systematic reviews and meta-analyses in responsible and governed ways, keeping researchers in the loop. Through hands-on exercises, the course emphasizes rigorous research methods, source verification, reproducibility, and human oversight, helping researchers use AI to accelerate their work without compromising scholarly standards.

The course includes four seminars that can be taken individually or together:
AI for Literature Reviews <https://instats.org/seminar/ai-for-literature-reviews>AI for Data Analysis <https://instats.org/seminar/ai-for-data-analysis>AI for Writing Research Papers <https://instats.org/seminar/ai-for-writing-research-papers>AI for Meta-Analysis <https://instats.org/seminar/ai-for-meta-analysis>
Sign up today <https://instats.org/course/ai-for-writing-papers-and-analyzing-data1>, and please feel free to share this opportunity with colleagues and students who might benefit!


